    "created_at": "2026-07-01T14:37:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-01T14:37:51Z",
    "body": "I wonder if it would be possible to replace the two first bullet points with checking that the resulting URL from [select an image source](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#selecting-an-image-source) is null.\n\nThe two initial bulletpoints, for reference:\n> - both the src attribute and the srcset attribute are omitted;\n> - the srcset attribute is omitted and the src attribute's value is the empty string;\n\nI've listed the result of the following checks below\n- checking that the URL returned by `select an image source` is null\n- checking the two first bulletpoints (current spec)\n- inserting the example in the DOM with `innerHTML` and checking `el.complete` in Gecko, Blink and WebKit\n\n| Example                                                          | `select an image source`  URL check | Current attribute check | Gecko | Blink | WebKit | \n| ------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------|-----------------|--------|-----|--------|\n| `<img />`                                                                                                | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<img src=\"\">`                                                                                      | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<img srcset=\"\">`                                                                                 | ✅                                 | ❌                      | ❌        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><img></picture>`                                                                | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><img src=\"\"></picture>`                                                    | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><source><img></picture>`                                                | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><source srcset=\"\"><img></picture>`.                              | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><source srcset=\"url\" type=\"print\"><img></picture>`    | ✅                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ✅  | ✅       |\n| `<picture><source srcset=\"url\"><img></picture>`                          | ❌                                 | ✅                      | ✅        | ❌  | ❌       |\n\n\nI did take a peek at the WebKit implementation, and the way I understand it the it checks the `imageSourceURL` of the image element and sets `m_imageComplete` to true if the result is empty. Both WebKit and Blink are aligned here and give expected results, while Gecko seem to follow the standard.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
